<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Urhi-Teshub</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">13th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century-bce">13th century BCE</a> · Also known as Mursili III</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Urhi-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teshub">Teshub</a>, who reigned as Mursili III, was king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hittite-empire">Hittites</a> for several years in the early 13th century BCE, son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muwatalli-ii">Muwatalli II</a>. He moved the capital back from Tarhuntassa to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hattusa">Hattusa</a> but was overthrown by his uncle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hattusili-iii">Hattusili III</a> after a civil war. Sent into exile in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a>, he later fled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>, and his asylum there strained Hittite relations with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ramesses-ii">Ramesses II</a>.</p></div>
